        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6e599daf-ddf2-5e9b-8616-20a92fbc3781",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Andrey Zvyagintsev, Marvin Heemeyer, Mikhail Krichman, István Szabó, Henning Mankell, Sara Stridsberg\n- Films: Leviathan, The Return, The Banishment, Elena\n- Events: Marvin Heemeyer's 2004 bulldozer attack, Bergman Week 2011\n- Concepts: Naboth's Vineyard\n\nFacts:\n- On June 4, 2004, Marvin Heemeyer drove an armored bulldozer through Granby, Colorado, damaging 13 buildings and causing about $7 million in damage.\n- In 2011, Andrey Zvyagintsev, István Szabó, Henning Mankell, and Sara Stridsberg were guests at Bergman Week 2011.\n- Mikhail Krichman photographed all of Andrey Zvyagintsev's films, including The Return (2003), The Banishment (2007), Elena (2010), and Leviathan (2014).\n- Andrey Zvyagintsev said that Marvin Heemeyer's story inspired Leviathan and that he adapted it to a Russian setting.\n- Critics compared Leviathan to the biblical story of Naboth's Vineyard, in which a king seeks a subject's land and is urged by his queen to obtain it slyly.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "015d0e45-213d-59de-ba91-c6c9c252cbdd",
        "text": "Page: Leviathan (2014 film). Sentence: According to Zvyagintsev, the story of Marvin Heemeyer in the United States inspired him and it was adapted into a Russian setting, but critics compare the story to the more similar biblical story of Naboth's Vineyard, where a King vies for his subjects' land and is motivated by his Queen to obtain it in a sly manner.\nPage: Marvin Heemeyer. Sentence: On June 4, 2004, automobile muffler repair shop owner Marvin John Heemeyer drove his armored bulldozer through Granby, Colorado, damaging 13 buildings, with the cost of the damage rounding to an estimated $7 million.\nPage: Mikhail Krichman. Sentence: He photographed all of Andrey Zvyagintsev's films, including \"The Return\" (2003), \"The Banishment\" (2007), \"Elena\" (2010) and \"Leviathan\" (2014).\nPage: Bergman Week. Sentence: Guests at the Bergman Week 2011 were among others directors Andrey Zvyagintsev and István Szabó as well as Swedish authors Henning Mankell and Sara Stridsberg.",
